# Intent System

Spec: IntentSystem
Purpose:
  Define the Intent object — the starting point of the SDD execution loop.
  Human provides high-level intent (e.g., "Build refund functionality").
  AI does NOT start coding immediately; it creates an @intent.* object
  that captures the goal, scope, constraints, and unknowns. This intent
  then flows through requirement extraction, knowledge resolution,
  architecture constraints, and task graph generation.

Owns: intents/

## Intent Object Schema

  @intent.I44

  goal:
      add refund functionality

  scope:
      payment

  constraints:
      idempotent
      auditable

  unknowns:
      provider refund behavior

  status:
      DISCOVERING

  created:
      2026-09-01

## Intent Lifecycle

  DISCOVERING → PLANNED → EXECUTING → COMPLETED → ARCHIVED

## Intent → Requirements

  AI analyzes intent and extracts requirements:
    R1: user can request refund
    R2: refund must be idempotent
    R3: refund must be auditable
    R4: provider failure must be handled

## Intent → Knowledge Resolution

  For each requirement, query the knowledge graph:
    R2 → @concept.idempotency → @skill.idempotency

## Intent → Architecture

  Intent scope → architecture constraints:
    @intent.I44 (scope: payment)
    → @architecture.ddd
    → domain: Refund
    → application: RefundService
    → infrastructure: PaymentProvider

## Rules

  [INT-01] Intent ≠ Task. Intent is the high-level goal.
  [INT-02] AI MUST create @intent.* before generating any task graph.
  [INT-03] Intent MUST capture constraints and unknowns explicitly.
  [INT-04] Intent status MUST track progress through lifecycle.
  [INT-05] Intent MUST be linked to generated execution plan via @plan.*.

